        looks up the build once, leaving nothing for the endpoint to repeat
        when stick_runner_job_requests_before_rate_limit is disabled
          counts the request as unauthenticated, as on master, with one lookup from the endpoint
      method: :patch, path_suffix: "/trace", params: "trace", headers: {"Content-Range"=>"0-4"}, status: :accepted
        resolves the job token before the rate limiter counts the request
        looks up the build once, leaving nothing for the endpoint to repeat
        when stick_runner_job_requests_before_rate_limit is disabled
          counts the request as unauthenticated, as on master, with one lookup from the endpoint
  when the throttle cohort enforce flag is on
    blocks the request with a 429 from labkit, not Rack::Attack
  when the bypass header is set
    skips the throttle, is not blocked, and writes no bypass counter

Git LFS API and storage
  # order defined
  with projects
    behaves like LFS http requests
      when LFS is disabled globally
        download request
          behaves like LFS http 501 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to eq "Git LFS is not enabled on this GitLab server, contact your admin."
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 501 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to eq "Git LFS is not enabled on this GitLab server, contact your admin."
      unauthenticated
        download request
          behaves like LFS http 401 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "text/plain"
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 401 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "text/plain"
      without access
        download request
          behaves like LFS http 404 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 404 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
      with guest access
        download request
          behaves like LFS http 404 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 404 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
      with download permission
        download request
          behaves like LFS http 200 blob response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/octet-stream"
          when container does not exist
            behaves like LFS http 404 response
              behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
                is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 403 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to eq "Access forbidden. Check your access level."
      with upload permission
        upload request
          behaves like LFS http 200 response
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
      deprecated API
        when fetching LFS object using deprecated API
          behaves like deprecated request
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to eq "Server supports batch API only, please update your Git LFS client to version 1.0.1 and up."
        when handling LFS request using deprecated API
          behaves like deprecated request
            behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
              is expected to eq "Server supports batch API only, please update your Git LFS client to version 1.0.1 and up."
      project specific LFS settings
        LFS disabled in project
          when uploading
            behaves like LFS http 404 response
              behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
                is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
          when downloading
            behaves like LFS http 404 response
              behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
                is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
        LFS enabled in project
          when uploading
            behaves like LFS http 200 response
              behaves like LFS http expected response code and message
                is expected to match "application/vnd.git-lfs+json"
