Git LFS File Locking API
  # order defined
  Create File Lock endpoint
    when user does not have download permission
      returns a 404 response
    when user does not have upload permission
      returns a 403 response
    with an existent lock
      return an error message
      returns the existen lock
    without an existent lock
      creates the lock
  Listing File Locks endpoint
    returns the list of locked files
    when user does not have download permission
      returns a 404 response
    when user does not have upload permission
      returns a 403 response
  List File Locks for verification endpoint
    returns the list of locked files grouped by owner
    when user does not have download permission
      returns a 404 response
    when user does not have upload permission
      returns a 403 response
    when using deploy key with write access
      returns all locks as theirs since deploy keys cannot own locks
  Delete File Lock endpoint
    when user does not have download permission
      returns a 404 response
    when user does not have upload permission
      returns a 403 response
    with an existent lock
      deletes the lock
      returns the deleted lock
      when a maintainer uses force
        deletes the lock
  Current.organization resolution
    resolves the organization owning the repository from the URL path

MetricsController
  # order defined
  behaves like Base action controller
    security headers
      Cross-Security-Policy
        when configuring snowplow
          when snowplow is enabled
            adds snowplow to the csp
          when snowplow is enabled but host is not configured
            behaves like snowplow is not in the CSP
              does not add the snowplow collector hostname to the CSP
          when snowplow is disabled
            behaves like snowplow is not in the CSP
              does not add the snowplow collector hostname to the CSP

OAuth Tokens requests
  # order defined
  when there is already a token for the application
    allows cross origin for token info
    and the request is done by the resource owner
      with authorization code grant type
        issues a new token
        does not revoke previous token
      with refresh token grant type
        issues a new token
        revokes previous token
        expired refresh token
          issues a new token
          revokes previous token
        revoked refresh token
          does not issue a new token
  when there is no token stored for the application
    generates and returns a new token

OmniauthCallbacksController
  # order defined
  GET /users/auth/jwt/callback
    when the user is already signed in
      when the user has a JWT identity
        redirects to root path
      when the user does not have a JWT identity
        redirects to identities path to receive user authorization before linking the identity
  sign-in when the email matches an existing account and auto_link is disabled
    redirects to sign-in, stashes the pending identity, and does not create a user
    lands on the identity authorization page once the user signs in
    when the failure is not an email collision
      falls back to the 422 failure page and does not stash an identity (FAILED - 182)
  #saml
    with IdP initiated request
      sets the metadata of the request in the context

OpenID Connect requests
  # order defined
  Application without OpenID scope
    token response does not include an ID token
    userinfo response is unauthorized
  Application with OpenID scope
    token response includes an ID token
    UserInfo payload
      includes all user information and group memberships
      does not include any unknown claims
      includes email and email_verified claims
      has public email in email claim
      has true in email_verified claim
    ID token payload
      includes the subject claims
      includes the GitLab root URL
      includes the time of the last authentication
      has public email in email claim
      has true in email_verified claim
      does not include any unknown properties
      does include groups
    when user has no first or last name
      omits both given_name and family_name from the userinfo response
      omits both given_name and family_name from the ID token
    when user is blocked
      redirects to login page
    when user is ldap_blocked
      redirects to login page
    OpenID Discovery keys
      with a cross-origin request
        returns data
        behaves like cross-origin GET request
          allows cross-origin request
      with a cross-origin preflight OPTIONS request
        behaves like cross-origin GET request
          allows cross-origin request
    OpenID WebFinger endpoint
      with a cross-origin request
        returns data
        behaves like cross-origin GET request
          allows cross-origin request
    with a cross-origin preflight OPTIONS request
      behaves like cross-origin GET request
        allows cross-origin request
  OpenID configuration information
    correctly returns the configuration
    with a cross-origin request
      behaves like cross-origin GET request
        allows cross-origin request
    with a cross-origin preflight OPTIONS request
      behaves like cross-origin GET request
        allows cross-origin request
  Application with OpenID and email scopes
    token response includes an ID token
    UserInfo payload
      includes the email and email_verified claims
      has private email in email claim
      has true in email_verified claim
      with a cross-origin request
        behaves like cross-origin GET and POST request
          allows cross-origin request
      with a cross-origin POST request
        behaves like cross-origin GET and POST request
          allows cross-origin request
      with a cross-origin preflight OPTIONS request
        behaves like cross-origin GET and POST request
          allows cross-origin request
    ID token payload
      has private email in email claim
      has true in email_verified claim
      does include groups

